<title>USA: C-Cube's DVD Decoders to be used by Packard Bell.</title>
<headline>C-Cube's DVD Decoders to be used by Packard Bell.</headline>
<dateline>MILPITAS, Calif. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>C-Cube Microsystems Inc said Diamond Multimedia's C-Cube based Digital Video Disc board will be incorporated into Packard Bell's new line of Platinum and Multimedia personal computers.</p>
<p>In a statement, C-Cube said Diamond's new PCI-based DVD board leverages C-Cube's single-chip ZiVA DVD decoder with integrated SecureView CSS copy protection and decryption technology to provide OEMs with a robust DVD decoder that supports all copy-protected Hollywood titles.</p>
</text>
